<!--
  Sanitized snapshot of a real Revolut Business EUR CAMT.053 statement (camt.053.001.08),
  trimmed to four entries that drive the v0.0.14 FeeSplitter feature. Built from the real
  2025 EUR statement the maintainer provided; PII removed, math preserved.

  Sanitization (PII removed, math preserved):
    - Account holder name / address / org-id replaced with generic placeholders
    - Counterparty natural-person names replaced with "Test User One"
    - Account IBAN replaced with an all-zero IBAN (still valid format)
    - Card PAN partially-masked digits replaced with 400000...0001
    - Free-text labels rewritten to neutral descriptions
  Kept verbatim (no PII, load-bearing for FeeSplitter / verification math):
    - All amounts, dates, currency codes, FX rates
    - All AcctSvcrRef / MsgId / Stmt Id (opaque hashes, no semantic content)
    - Balance blocks (OPBD/CLBD), TxsSummry totals, and every <Chrgs> block

  Why EUR (not the CHF Jan-May fixture): the cross-currency-fee guard can only be shown
  on an account whose currency differs from the fee currency. An EUR->CHF own-account
  transfer posts a EUR amount but a CHF fee, which is exactly the case that must NOT split.

  Entries and the FeeSplitter case each one drives:
    - 2025-05-13  ref 6822efa8...  EUR 200.00 DBIT, fee 1.12 CHF  -> cross-currency: NO split
    - 2025-03-02  ref 67c3499d...  EUR  67.33 DBIT, fee 0.67 EUR  -> same-currency split (-66.66 / -0.67)
    - 2025-02-02  ref 679e4513...  EUR  77.05 DBIT, fee 0.76 EUR  -> same-currency split (-76.29 / -0.76)
    - 2025-11-14  ref 6916be67...  EUR 250.00 CRDT, no fee        -> plain entry (single line)

  Internal-consistency check (verifiable by hand):
    OPBD 1000.00 + TtlNetNtry -94.38 = CLBD 905.62
    TtlCdtNtries.Sum 250.00 - TtlDbtNtries.Sum 344.38 = -94.38
    NbOfNtries 4 = 1 credit + 3 debit
    TtlNtries.Sum 594.38 = 250.00 + 344.38
  Note: <Amt> is fee-inclusive (the posted movement), so the debit Amts already contain
  their fees; the summary totals are computed from those posted Amts, not from principals.
-->
